# Header + Tabs UI Pattern

Use for pages with multiple sub-sections (e.g. settings pages, detail pages with tabs) where a full-width header bar contains navigation tabs.

## Structure

- **Full-width header**: `w-full border-b bg-muted/30`
- **Tabs live inside the header**: Use `TabsList` + `TabsTrigger` from `@engenty/ui-core` with `variant="line"`
- **Tab content**: Separate section below, centered with `max-w-*` and `p-page`

## Layout Contract

```
<Tabs className="flex w-full flex-col" defaultValue="...">
  <header className="w-full shrink-0 border-b bg-muted/30">
    <div className="mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-end px-4 pt-3 pb-0 md:px-5">
      <TabsList variant="line" className="-mb-px w-fit border-0 bg-transparent p-0">
        <TabsTrigger value="...">...</TabsTrigger>
      </TabsList>
    </div>
  </header>
  <div className="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl flex-1 space-y-6 p-page">
    <TabsContent value="...">...</TabsContent>
  </div>
</Tabs>
```

## Stacked sections under tabs

- For blocks that look like **Appearance** settings (section title, muted description, then a bordered form card), use **`SettingsFormSection`** from `@engenty/ui-core` (see `settings-form-section-ui.mdc`).

## Key Details

- **Header padding**: `pt-3 pb-0` — no bottom padding so the active tab underline aligns flush with the gray `border-b`
- **Items alignment**: `items-end` so tabs and their underline sit at the bottom of the header
- **Tabs variant**: Use `variant="line"` — underline-style tabs, not button-like segmented controls
- **TabsList overrides**: `border-0 bg-transparent p-0` when inside the header; `-mb-px` helps the blue underline meet the gray line

## Tabs Component (ui-core)

- For underline-style tabs: `TabsList variant="line"`
- Do not use `variant="segmented"` when you want tab styling (it renders button-like pill controls)
- Reference: `packages/ai-ui/src/routes/ai-settings-page.tsx`
